      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "OUR MAJOR JACK NZ (12) turned in a good effort at his latest run to get home by a narrow margin over 2130m at Gloucester Park on August 4. May just need a bit of luck at some point from this difficult draw. Meets a comparable field so he is capable of getting the job done again. GALVINSTON JOHN (1) finished sixth at Gloucester Park two runs ago before finishing fifth at his latest appearance over 2130m at Gloucester Park, beaten 12 metres. Will enjoy a nice run from this favourable starting position. Meets a similar quality field and is good enough to win a race of this calibre. JOEY JAMES (10) has been thereabouts of late and is a great chance to break through. Good effort last time out when he finished second at this track over 2185m. A DUKE TO BE (9) is in the mix after turning in a better effort last start to finish third at Gloucester Park over 2130m.",
